  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'a) The prestige that Gongsa Ugyen Wangchuck earned abroad not only helped to deepen Bhutan''s relations with British India and Tibet, but also reinforced his own leadership position within the country. Critically assess and explain the role played by Gongsa Ugyen Wangchuck and the circumstances that led to the creation of the Hereditary Monarchy in Bhutan. (10 marks)', 'a) Circumstances: by the 19th century the dual system established by Zhabdrung had weakened; Desis changed frequently and powerful regional governors fought each other, leaving Bhutan in civil war and vulnerable to external powers (e.g. the Duar War with British India, 1864-65). Role of Ugyen Wangchuck: as Trongsa Penlop (Gongsa) he defeated his rivals at the Battle of Changlimithang in 1885, ending civil war and bringing peace and unity. Externally, he skilfully balanced relations with British India and Tibet; during the British expedition to Lhasa (1903-04) he acted as mediator, earning the respect of the British, who knighted him (KCIE) in 1905. This international prestige, together with his success at home in restoring order and his piety and generosity, made him the natural leader of the country. On 17 December 1907, at Punakha, the monastic body, officials and representatives of the people unanimously chose him as the first hereditary King and signed a genja (oath of allegiance). Critically, the monarchy arose from a genuine national need for stability and from his proven leadership, not from conquest alone.', null, '[{"point": "Circumstances: weakened dual system, civil wars among Penlops/ Dzongpons, need for stable central authority; Ugyen Wangchuck''s victory at Changlimithang (1885) and unification", "marks": 4}, {"point": "External role: mediation in British-Tibet conflict (Younghusband expedition 1903-04), KCIE 1905, good relations with British India secured sovereignty; this prestige strengthened his position; unanimous election and enthronement 17 December 1907 at Punakha with genja", "marks": 6}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development') and t.slug = 'history-the-monarchy'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-general-3'), 'standard', 10,
    1080, 'historical_official', 'awaiting_review',
    null, null,
