  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'b) In just 15 years as King and Head of State, His Majesty The King has transformed the aspirations of the people into achievements. His Majesty continues to work tirelessly to ensure that the people of Bhutan are not deprived of anything that the citizens of developed countries can access. Discuss some of the most important achievements and transformations brought about by His Majesty The King for the wellbeing of the country and the Bhutanese people. (10 marks)', 'b) Achievements of His Majesty King Jigme Khesar Namgyel Wangchuck: (1) Kidu - granting land kidu and resolving land issues, citizenship and welfare kidu, personally reaching the poorest; (2) De-suung (2011), training thousands of volunteers who serve in disasters and national events, and Gyalsung, national service for youth; (3) exceptional leadership during COVID-19 - personally travelling to high-risk areas, the Druk Gyalpo''s Relief Kidu for those who lost income, and one of the world''s fastest vaccination campaigns; (4) Royal Kashos on education reform (2020) and civil service reform (2020), driving transformation towards excellence; (5) nurturing the young democracy - guiding institutions and reminding citizens of their duties; (6) leading disaster relief and reconstruction after earthquakes and floods; (7) championing youth, the elderly and the vulnerable, and Bhutan''s international standing. Through these His Majesty has turned aspirations into achievements.', null, '[{"point": "Achievements of the Fifth King: kidu - land kidu and land reforms, citizenship and welfare kidu; De-suung (2011) and Gyalsung; leadership in COVID-19 (Druk Gyalpo''s Relief Kidu, vaccination); Royal Kashos on education and civil service reform; strengthening democracy and institutions; disaster response (2009, 2011 earthquakes); support for elderly and youth", "marks": 10}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
