  values ('ME', 'analytical', 'With the decline in Foreign Currency Reserves (FCR), the Government has issued a moratorium on the import of vehicles. Discuss the importance of having adequate FCR and suggest other additional measures that would help the government protect or enhance FCR. (20 marks)', 'Importance of adequate foreign currency reserves: (1) Bhutan imports most of its fuel, food, medicines, machinery and consumer goods, which must be paid for in Indian rupees or US dollars; (2) reserves are needed to service external debt, mostly hydropower loans; (3) they maintain confidence in the ngultrum and its peg to the Indian rupee; (4) they act as a buffer against shocks such as pandemics, disasters or a fall in hydropower revenue; (5) Article 14 of the Constitution requires the government to maintain reserves sufficient to meet at least one year of essential imports; and (6) healthy reserves support Bhutan''s creditworthiness.
Additional measures to protect or enhance reserves: (1) increase exports - complete hydropower projects on time, and promote exports of minerals, agricultural products (cardamom, oranges, potatoes), processed goods and services; (2) import substitution - grow more food at home, support local manufacturing and cottage industries; (3) discourage non-essential and luxury imports through higher taxes or temporary restrictions; (4) attract foreign direct investment and encourage remittances from Bhutanese abroad through incentives and convenient channels; (5) revive high-value tourism to earn convertible currency; (6) reduce fuel imports through electric vehicles, public transport and energy efficiency; (7) manage credit growth so loans do not fuel excessive imports; (8) borrow prudently; and (9) promote ''Made in Bhutan'' products and spending on domestic goods.', null, '[{"point": "Importance: pay for essential imports (fuel, food, medicines), service external debt, maintain ngultrum-rupee peg and confidence, buffer against shocks, constitutional requirement of at least 12 months essential imports (Article 14), credit rating", "marks": 8}, {"point": "Additional measures: boost exports (hydropower, minerals, agriculture, tourism), import substitution (food, local products), restrict/ tax luxury imports, promote FDI and remittances (incentives, NRB accounts), encourage domestic production, manage credit growth for imports, energy efficiency/ EVs to reduce fuel imports, prudent borrowing, monitor rupee/ USD reserves", "marks": 12}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development') and t.slug = 'foreign-currency-reserves'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-general-3'), 'standard', 20,
